{"id": "samsung_elec-2026-11-18-005", "date": "2026-11-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": ["samsung_elec"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": [], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Samsung Begins One UI 9.5 Beta Program", "content": "Samsung has launched the One UI 9.5 beta program, giving users an early look at One UI 9.5 ahead of its official debut. The One UI 9.5 beta introduces more precise camera controls, personalized health insights, improved accessibility features, and stronger privacy protections for everyday use. Enhanced Pro and Pro video modes put finer settings […]", "sources": [{"name": "samsung_elec", "url": "https://news.samsung.com/global/samsung-begins-one-ui-9-5-beta-program", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "lg_elec-2026-11-18-006", "date": "2026-11-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": ["lg_elec", "samsung_elec", "lg_display"], "customers": ["lg_elec", "samsung_elec"], "suppliers": ["lg_display"]}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["mass production"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["多公司提及", "供應鏈上下游同時提及"]}, "title": "Samsung Display and LG Display to start producing panels for Apple's iPhone 18 and iPhone Air 2", "content": "<p>According to reports from Korea, <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/samsung-oled\">Samsung Display</a> and <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/lg-oled\">LG Display</a> are both getting ready to start producing the AMOLED displays for Apple's standard iPhone 18 and its iPhone Air 2, which are expected to launch in March 2027. LG Display will start mass production in late December 2026, and Samsung Display in January 2027. This year Apple split its iPhone 18 launch in two: in September it <a href=", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/samsung-display-and-lg-display-start-producing-panels-apples-spring-2027-iphone", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "samsung_elec-2026-11-18-007", "date": "2026-11-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": ["samsung_elec"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration", "automotive_display"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "SFC withdraws its IPO a day before the public subscription, reveals it lost the blue dopant slot in Samsung's latest IT OLED material set", "content": "<p>Korea-based blue OLED emitter maker <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/sun-fine-chem\">SFC</a> (Sun Fine Chem) withdrew its planned IPO on Korea's KOSPI exchange, a day before the public subscription was set to begin. SFC says that after it completed the demand forecast with institutional investors (held on November 9-13), it decided together with its underwriters to cancel the offering, as it is currently difficult for the company to receive a fair valuation.</p><a href=\"https://www.oled-info", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/sfc-withdraws-its-ipo-day-public-subscription-its-filing-reveals-it-lost-blue", "type": "rss"}]}
